<!DOCTYPE suzuki [
<!ENTITY % sdatacharaents SYSTEM "..\config8\sdatacharaents.txt">
%sdatacharaents;
]>
<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "1E">
<servcat sctnbr = "01" scnbr = "05">
<configtype typenbr = "1">
<servinfotype sitcode = "4">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A1514001" svcinfotypenbr = "06" svcinfoqualnbr = "01" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Oil Pressure Check
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Before checking oil pressure, check the following points.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Oil level in oil pan
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If oil level is low, add oil up to FULL level mark (hole) (1) on oil level gauge. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1516001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
<figure page = "2">
<graphic graphicname = "IYSQ01020012.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "45.200mm" ver = "01" gw = "160" gh = "111"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "2" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
2.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
LOW level mark (hole)
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Oil quality
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If oil is discolored or deteriorated, change it. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1516001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Oil leakage
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If leakage is found, repair leaky point.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<s1>
<ptxt>
For M/T model, place gear shift lever in “Neutral” and apply parking brake.
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
For A/T model, place select lever in “P” and apply parking brake.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove oil pressure switch. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1516003"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install special tools to threaded hole where oil pressure switch was removed.
</ptxt>
<servicetool>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1E101">
<s-part>
(A)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09915-77311">
09915–77311
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
<servicetoolitem id = "L1E102">
<s-part>
(B)
</s-part>
<s-number num = "09915-78211">
09915–78211
</s-number>
</servicetoolitem>
</servicetool>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFAE0A150028.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "62.425mm" ver = "01" gw = "203" gh = "160"/>
</figure>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Start engine and warm it up to normal operating temperature.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Measure oil pressure at 1,500 rpm and 4,000 rpm respectively.
</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>
Oil pressure specification
</title>
<ptxt>
110 – 190 kPa (1.1 – 1.9 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, 16.0 – 27.6 psi, 1.1 – 1.9 bar) at 1,500 rpm
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
310 – 390 kPa (3.2 – 4.0 kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>, 45.0 – 56.6 psi, 3.1 – 3.9 bar) at 4,000 rpm
</ptxt>
</spec>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Stop engine and remove special tools.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Install oil pressure switch. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1516003"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Check DTC. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1114003"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
<ptxt>
If any DTC is displayed, clear DTC. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1114004"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Start engine and check oil pressure switch for oil leakage.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfo>
</servinfotype>
</configtype>
</servcat>
</section></manual></suzuki>
